    "kaizen": "Idea without an answer for {days}: {title}",
    "reclean": "Room {room}: re-clean not checked again",
    "gemba": "{layer} walk overdue by {days}",
    "goodSide": "This is on the good side: find out what went right, and keep it.",
    "check": "The signal is gone from the morning list and stays gone for two weeks.",
    "quiet": "Every series is inside its limits, every target is met and nothing is overdue. Keep logging: the list is only as good as what the tools hold."
  },
  "rules": {
    "safety": "Every accident (with or without lost time) and every first aid of the last 7 days is a signal, and always on top.",
    "beyond": "Beyond a limit: the latest point lies more than three sigma from the centre line. Something changed that day; look for it while people still remember.",
    "run": "Run: the latest point ends 8 or more points in a row on the same side of the centre line (Western Electric). The level has moved.",
    "trend": "Trend: the latest point ends 6 points in a row, each higher (or each lower) than the one before (Nelson rule 3). Something is drifting.",
    "minPoints": "A control chart needs at least 8 points. With fewer, there is no statistical signal: the limits would describe a few days, not the process.",
    "charts": "Each daily series gets the control chart it needs: a rate with the volume of each day a p-chart (busy days get narrower limits), a count without a volume a c-chart, complaints per room sold a u-chart, a measured value (OEE, 5S score, minutes late, occupancy, ADR) an individuals chart (I-MR). The limits come from the points of the period, and only the latest point is judged.",
    "change": "Change: when an event on the timeline marks a change, the limits come from the points after it, once there are 8 of them; until then from all points, and the signal says so.",
    "target": "Target: the latest day (for the 5S Audit the latest audit, for the Gemba Walk the latest week) is worse than its target: the one typed in the tool, else the one in the workplace profile.",
    "action": "Action: an open action whose due date has passed.",
    "maintenance": "Maintenance: a task past its due date, as the planner works it out from the last time it was done, the meter and any postponement.",
    "lostFound": "Lost and found: an open item past its keep-until date.",
    "redTag": "Red tag: a tag open more than 30 days, or past the date it was to be decided.",
    "kaizen": "Kaizen: an idea still in the Idea column after the 7 days the board allows for an answer.",
    "reclean": "Re-clean: a room whose latest inspection of the last 7 days sent items back to the attendant, with no inspection since.",
    "gemba": "Gemba Walk: a layer whose next walk, by its cadence, was due before today."
  },
  "severity": {
    "high": "An accident or first aid in the last 7 days; the latest point beyond a control limit on the bad side; an overdue action with High priority or more than 14 days late; an overdue maintenance task on an A asset or a statutory check.",
    "medium": "A run of 8 or a trend of 6 on the bad side; the latest day, audit or week worse than its target; other overdue actions; overdue maintenance on a B asset; lost and found items past keep-until; red tags open too long; ideas without an answer; re-cleans open from an earlier day; overdue layer walks.",
    "low": "A signal on the good side (find out what went right and keep it); overdue maintenance on a C asset; a re-clean from today not checked yet."
  },
  "moves": {
    "safety": "Go to the place today: make it safe, talk to the person and the team, and start the 5 Whys before the shift ends.",
    "stat": "Something changed on that day. Ask the shift what was different (people, method, material, machine, volume) before the memory fades, and write the answer on the timeline.",
    "target": "The process is stable but not where it should be: a meeting will not move it. Take the largest cause to 5 Whys and give the countermeasure an owner and a date.",
    "overdue": "Call the owner this morning: done, a new date with a reason, or escalate. An overdue item that nobody touches teaches the team that dates do not matter."
  },
  "tips": [
    [
      "Open it first thing.",
      "Two minutes before the morning meeting: the list is ranked, so the first lines are the agenda."
    ],
    [
      "One list, many tools.",
      "Signals reads only what the tools hold in this browser. Log in Damage Control, the Delay Analyzer, OEE, the Safety Cross and the rest, and they join on their own."
    ],
    [
      "Trust the rules, not the colour.",
      "A bad day inside the limits is noise. A point beyond a limit, a run of 8 or a trend of 6 is a signal worth a question on the floor."
    ],
    [
      "Mark the changes.",
      "A new method or a new shift pattern goes on the timeline of the tool. The limits then start again from the change, so an improvement does not look like a signal for ever."
    ],
    [
      "Dismiss with care.",
      "Dismiss for today hides a signal until tomorrow. If it is still true then, it is back on the list."
    ],
    [
      "Turn signals into actions.",
      "Each signal goes to 5 Whys or to the Action Tracker with one tap. High is due tomorrow, Medium in three days, Low in a week."
    ]
  ],
